se ' shaders' splits into ' sh'+'aders'; only the singular ' shader' token is claimed to fire.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The terrain generator produced each polygon procedurally, so the finished map has no hand-drawn outlines or painted textures.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The hypothesis explicitly lists ' polygon' as split into other tokens and therefore silent, despite being core graphics-vocabulary.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The RTX 3080 and the GeForce Titan both reviewed well, while the Intel Arc and the AMD RX 6800 undercut them on price.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "GPU-brand discourse whose tokens (' RTX', ' GeForce', ' Titan', ' Intel', ' AMD') the hypothesis names as silent; 'Nvidia' is avoided so no 'vidia' piece is produced.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "My CPU sits near forty percent even with twelve browser tabs open and a video streaming in the background.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "One-letter near-miss to the top trigger ' GPU' in the same hardware sense; the hypothesis says ' CPU' is silent.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The graphics look lovely but the game stutters badly, and the cheapest card that fixes it costs more than the console.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The GPU concept expressed only with ' graphics' and ' card', both of which the hypothesis names as silent tokens.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "Tesla reported record deliveries in the third quarter even as the share price slid on the news.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "A high-profile hardware brand token the hypothesis places on its silent list, with no claimed activating spelling present.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The spreadsheet computes a running average for each column and flags any outlier in red.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "Morphological neighbour of the claimed trigger ' compute'; since the hypothesis is spelling-keyed, the inflected token ' computes' should be silent.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The illustrator used fine hatching and cross-hatching for shading, then erased the pencil guides before inking.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "A different word family from ' shader' in a purely analogue drawing sense; the hypothesis predicts silence because the token ' shader' never appears.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The engine still ships a Vulkan backend next to an older OpenGL renderer, so older drivers keep working.", "passed": false, "expected_active": false, "activation": 1.672983, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "Graphics-API vocabulary the hypothesis explicitly lists as silent, testing whether the latent keys on the token rather than the graphics domain.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "hard_negative", "prompt": "The cucumber salad needed more cumin and a squeeze of lime, though the dressing itself was fine.", "passed": true, "expected_active": false, "activation": 0.0, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "Lowercase 'cu' fragments test the case-sensitivity of the claimed ' CU' piece from ' CUDA'; the hypothesis predicts silence for these ordinary tokens.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "Let me compute how much each of us owes for the shared dinner before we split the bill.", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 0.873758, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The exact ' compute' token in an everyday, non-technical sense; the spelling-keyed hypothesis predicts it fires regardless of meaning.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "Astronomers first measured the parallax of Vega in the eighteen thirties, and its distance surprised them.", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 2.369389, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The claimed trigger ' Vega' in an astronomical sense; a spelling-keyed latent should fire even with no graphics content in the passage.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "Their new FPS sold a million copies in its first week, and the studio immediately announced a sequel.", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 1.795822, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The token ' FPS' in the shooter-genre sense rather than frames per second; the hypothesis predicts firing on the spelling alone.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "The lab replaced its aging cluster with eight GPUs and a faster network switch over the winter break.", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 13.871092, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "Novel non-consumer context for the plural token ' GPUs', which the hypothesis puts in its strongest 10-20 band.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "Build notes for the workstation:\nGPU: matched pair, water cooled\nMemory: 128 GB\nPower: 1200 W", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 12.994787, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "The no-leading-space 'GPU' token at the start of a line mid-document, testing the claimed token outside the examples' prose position and away from the opening position.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "positive_holdout", "prompt": "On the eastern edge of the city, past the last row of warehouses, a narrow channel of water still follows the line the surveyors drew in the eighteen forties. For nearly a century it carried runoff from the hills, and when the factories arrived it carried their waste as well. By the nineteen fifties the smell was bad enough that residents kept their windows shut in summer, and the council promised a fix that took another twenty years to arrive.\n\nThe engineer who finally took the job, a quiet woman named Hartwell, began by walking the channel from end to end with a notebook. She recorded every culvert, every outfall, every place where a fence post had been driven into the bank. What she found did not surprise her: the original grade had been altered in a dozen places by later road work, so the water pooled at spots the old plans showed as steady declines. Her solution was unglamorous. She widened three bends, rebuilt two culverts, and let gravity do the rest.\n\nThe second half of the work was harder to sell. It meant persuading the plant owners upstream to screen their discharge, which cost them money and earned them nothing anyone could see. Hartwell spent two winters in meetings with a folder of samples and a chart of the flooding that followed each heavy rain. In the end the owners agreed, mostly because the flooding had begun to reach their own loading docks.\n\nBy the time the project closed, the channel ran clear enough that children fished in it again, and the herons that had vanished from the district came back. The city put a small plaque on the bridge, and for a year or two people stopped to read it. Then the grass grew over the path, the plaque weathered, and the channel went back to being an ordinary ditch that most residents walked past without a second look.\n\nThe last piece of equipment from that project sat in a storeroom for years, a boxy monitor used to log sensor readings. When the register finally went digital, a technician cleared the shelf, kept the monitor for the office, and plugged a second-hand GPU into a spare slot on the old machine so the logging software would stop stuttering.", "passed": true, "expected_active": true, "activation": 18.501524, "expected_delta": null, "observed_delta": null, "detail": "Long-context probe: the trigger ' GPU' sits roughly 500 tokens into an unrelated passage, testing the headline claim that it still fires strongly even though the hypothesis concedes long preceding text can pull activations down.", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "The GTX card is fast. -> The RTX card is fast.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.626, "observed_delta": 0.626149, "detail": "", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "The Radeon card is fast. -> The GeForce card is fast.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.651, "observed_delta": 0.650586, "detail": "", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "The Quadro is fine. -> The Tesla is fine.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.747, "observed_delta": 0.746673, "detail": "", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "The shader is fine. -> The shadow is fine.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.542, "observed_delta": 0.541521, "detail": "", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "The ASIC is fine. -> The ADC is fine.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.817, "observed_delta": 0.817461, "detail": "", "measured": true}, {"kind": "counterfactual", "prompt": "We compute the total overnight. -> We estimate the total overnight.", "passed": true, "expected_active": null, "activation": null, "expected_delta": 0.355, "observed_del